{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he took for himself all these.</b> The Rabbis say: He also showed him the tenth of an ephah. It is said here <b>all these</b>, and it is said elsewhere: ״והבאת את המנחה אשר יעשה מאלה״ (and you shall bring the meal-offering that is made of these)." "<b>And he split them.</b> One may say: such is the way of offerings, to cut them into pieces, as it is written: ״ונתח אותה״ etc. (and he shall cut it into pieces)." "<b>But the bird he did not split.</b> For there is in it only splitting (שיסוע) and not dividing, because they are small and the pieces would be too small and not fit for anything." "Another interpretation: <b>And he split them.</b> It was necessary to place from the animals half split from this side and half split from that side, because from each species there were three. <b>But the bird he did not split</b> — there were two, and he could leave them whole, one here and one there."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:19.482527816Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}